| `tests.isolation.tiers.<tier>.writes` | string | `temp` for every tier | a tier marker name mapped to `temp` or `any`: a closed set | `tests/isolation_guard.py` (`load_policy`), installed by `tests/conftest.py` | Sets where a test of the tier may create, change or remove a file, directory or link, change its mode, owner, flags, times or extended attributes, or bind an AF_UNIX socket to a path: `temp` allows only `tests.scratch_root` and pytest's basetemp (a bytecode file in a `__pycache__` and the null device aside), and `any` allows anywhere. A metadata change through a link is judged at the link and at its target, except when `shutil`'s own copy says it stays on the link, so `shutil.copytree(..., symlinks=True)` of a tree holding a link that points outside is allowed. A test with no marker this block names gets `temp`. | reading a file, which only `tests.isolation.tiers.<tier>.stores` judges, for a listed store | always |
